Landscape menu is missing title entirely because header hidden; not ideal. At 844x390, there is plenty horizontal space but not vertical. Could show a compact logo smaller, maybe 30px height, rather than hide. The menu-panel starts y76, top 56; could add a small logo above panel using font-size 36, tagline hidden. Would add ~45px; total content 323, still fits within 374 (96vh). The current menu-inner y56 h278; adding 50 -> 328, y31, fits. We can improve by not hiding header entirely but compacting:
```
@media (max-height: 560px) {
  .menu-header { margin-top: 0; }
  .logo { font-size: clamp(30px, 8vh, 46px); }
  .tagline { display: none; }
  .menu-inner { gap: 10px; padding: 8px 10px; }
  .menu-panel { ... }
  .menu-footer { ... maybe display none? }
}
```
At 390 height, logo 8vh=31px, width 226, fits above panel. Header height ~28. Total y maybe 38. This looks better. Instead of hiding. Or keep title for landscape. User expects polished. Let's implement compact header.

At 844x390, the menu's content: header 31px + panel 214 + footer 12 + gaps 2*10 + padding 16 = 283; fits 374. Good.

At 320x480 (if landscape), logo 30px, panel 214, footer 12 + 20 gaps = 276 + padding 16=292, fits 480. Good.

So replace media max-height 560 to:
```
@media (max-height: 560px) {
  .menu-inner { gap: 10px; padding: 8px 10px; }
  .menu-header { margin-top: 0; }
  .logo { font-size: clamp(28px, 8vh, 44px); }
  .tagline { display: none; }
  .controls-card { display:none; }
  .menu-footer { display:none? } // keep maybe
}
```
The existing media also hides controls and sets gap 12. We'll replace.

Would the header take vertical space but still fit? yes.

